    "description": "The player chasing a number. Modifiers and stats first, a second Action only when there is nowhere left to put a modifier, and Triggers last of all. Not a strawman — it is the commonest way a real run goes wrong, and it is the policy that reproduced the trigger famine: measured on the curated library it burned every Trigger out of its own pool by refusal and finished on one live row.",
